I have heard that many Danes volunteer in their free time.
I like the idea.
I want to learn to speak better Danish and meet new people.
One evening, I am sitting with my computer.
I find a website for voluntary work.
I read the first three listings on the site.
The first listing is from a sports club.
But they need help on Thursday evenings, and I play badminton then.
The second listing is from a museum.
They need a person on Wednesday evenings, but I work out then.
Then I look at the third listing.
It is from the little café that I already know.
They need people for Saturday mornings.
That suits me absolutely perfectly.
I fill in a short form with my name and my email address.
I also write my phone number: twelve, thirty-four, fifty-six, seventy-eight.
Finally, I press send.
I have never worked in a café before, but I am ready to learn it.
